.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt EVP_RAND-CRNG-TEST 7ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm EVP_RAND-CRNG-TEST
.Nd The FIPS health testing EVP_RAND filter
.Sh DESCRIPTION
This
.Sy EVP_RAND
object acts as a filter between the entropy source and its users.
It performs CRNG health tests as defined in
.Lk https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/sp/800/90/b/final
Section 4 "Health Tests".
Most requests are forwarded to the entropy source, either via its parent
reference or via the provider entropy upcalls.
.Ss Identity
"CRNG-TEST" is the name for this implementation; it can be used with the
.Xr EVP_RAND_fetch 3
function.
.Ss Supported parameters
If a parent EVP_RAND is specified on context creation, the parent's
parameters are supported because the request is forwarded to the parent
seed source for processing.
.Pp
If no parent EVP_RAND is specified on context creation, the following
parameters are supported:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqstate" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STATE Ns ) <integer>
.It \(dqstrength" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_STRENGTH Ns ) <unsigned integer>
.It \(dqmax_request" ( Ns Sy OSSL_RAND_PARAM_MAX_REQUEST Ns ) <unsigned integer>
These parameters work as described in
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 .
.It \(dqfips-indicator" ( Ns Sy OSSL_DRBG_PARAM_FIPS_APPROVED_INDICATOR Ns ) <integer>
This parameter works as described in
.Xr provider-rand 7 .
.El
.Sh NOTES
This EVP_RAND is only implemented by the OpenSSL FIPS provider.
.Pp
A context for a health test filter can be obtained by calling:
.Bd -literal
 EVP_RAND *parent = ...;
 EVP_RAND *rand = EVP_RAND_fetch(NULL, "CRNG-TEST", NULL);
 EVP_RAND_CTX *rctx = EVP_RAND_CTX_new(rand, parent);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr EVP_RAND 3 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS 7
.Sh HISTORY
This functionality was added in OpenSSL 3.4.
